# Pull request descriptions (this workshop)

This project rule applies when this workshop folder is the Cursor workspace.
It wins over personal Goal / Ran / Doubt prefs when those conflict.

When you draft, create, or update a pull request **in this folder**:

| Section | Required | Content |
|---------|----------|---------|
| **What** | Yes | What changed in these workshop files |
| **Why this repo** | Yes | Why it belongs here, not in an application repo |
| **Verify** | Yes | How a participant or facilitator checks it |

Use headings `## What`, `## Why this repo`, and `## Verify`.

**Hard gate:** Do not use `## Goal`, `## Ran`, or `## Doubt` here.

Do not open or push a pull request unless the user explicitly asks.
This file is the Lab C contrast with personal Goal / Ran / Doubt.
